 ['Captive','An insurer owned by a non-insurance group to insure its own risks. Often reinsures through a fronting insurer.','Receives ceded premium from the fronting insurer.','A Reinsurance Party.'],
 ['Regulator','Sets solvency and reinsurance rules (for example IRDAI in India, MAS in Singapore, APRA in Australia, PRA in the UK, state regulators in the USA).','No money; sets capital credit for reinsurance and approved-reinsurer rules.','Drives credit rating data, cession rules and reports (not in source).']
